The '''2014–15 season''' was the 121st season of competitive football by [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]. They competed in the [[2014–15 Scottish Premiership|Scottish Premiership]], [[2014–15 Scottish League Cup|Scottish League Cup]] and [[2014–15 Scottish Cup|Scottish Cup]]. They also competed in the [[2014–15 UEFA Europa League|Europa League]], having been eliminated in the play-off round of the [[2014–15 UEFA Champions League|Champions League]].

On 6 June 2014, [[Ronny Deila]]<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/27718845 |title=Celtic confirm Ronny Deila as new manager |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=bbc.co.uk |date=6 June 2014 |access-date=28 July 2014}}</ref> was appointed as the club's new manager, succeeding [[Neil Lennon]] in the role.<ref>{{cite web|title=Neil Lennon ends his four-year spell as manager|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/27519596|work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=bbc.co.uk|access-date=22 May 2014|date=28 July 2014}}</ref>

